# Agentic SDLC

Follow `.cursor/skills/agentic-sdlc/SKILL.md` for the active step. The story input is `docs/user-story.md`, loaded by `python scripts/load_user_story.py` from Jira, Confluence, Word, or a local file.

This chat is the orchestrator. Delegate the active step to the sub-agent named in that skill. Show the handoff and wait. Do not write the step artifact in this chat, and do not start the next sub-agent before the user approves.

Each sub-agent writes its markdown in its own folder under `.cursor/artifacts/`, in order, and only after the previous one is approved. Never write these files at the repository root:

1. `.cursor/artifacts/requirements-agent/requirements.md` — after the user answers clarifying questions
2. `.cursor/artifacts/architect/architecture.md`
3. `.cursor/artifacts/design-reviewer/design-review.md`, then update `.cursor/artifacts/architect/architecture.md` for agreed changes
4. `.cursor/artifacts/planner/impl-plan.md` — dependency order, with blocked tasks named
5. One approved task at a time under `src/holdshelf` and `tests/`
6. `.cursor/artifacts/code-reviewer/code-review.md`
7. `.cursor/artifacts/verifier/verification-report.md`
8. `CHANGELOG.md` at the repository root and `.cursor/artifacts/release-agent/pull-request.md` — only when the user asks

Record unknown facts as `Not Found`. Do not skip a gate because a later prompt was pasted.

```markdown
# Bad
Rewrote the hold list endpoint because the story mentioned overdue holds.

# Good
Loaded HOLD-21 from Jira, asked the five open questions in docs/user-story.md,
and waited for answers before drafting the requirements.
```
